{"book":23,"chapter":17,"context":{"chapter":17,"title":"Damascus Becomes a Ruin","summary":"Damascus will become a heap of ruins, and its ally Israel (Ephraim) will be stripped like a gleaned field, though a few will turn to their Maker. The chapter closes with roaring nations scattered overnight like chaff.","background":"Damascus, capital of Aram (Syria), had joined Israel against Judah (chapter 7). Assyria captured it in 732 BC and deported its people (2 Kings 16:9). The valley of Rephaim (v. 5), southwest of Jerusalem, was fertile farmland where reapers and gleaners were a familiar sight.","customs":[{"term":"Gleaning the olive tree","verses":"17:6","note":"Olives were harvested by beating the branches; the few left at the top were for the poor (Deuteronomy 24:20). Israel will be reduced to a handful."},{"term":"Groves","verses":"17:8","note":"Asherah poles, wooden cult objects honoring the Canaanite goddess Asherah."}],"watchFor":["A turn to the Maker and the Holy One of Israel (v. 7).","'Pleasant plants… strange slips' (v. 10) may describe gardens planted for foreign gods.","Trouble at evening, gone by morning (v. 14)."],"connections":["2 Kings 16:9","Deuteronomy 24:20","Amos 1:3-5","2 Kings 19:35"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["מַשָּׂא","masa'","H4853","HNcmsc","[the] oracle of"],["דַּמָּשֶׂק","damasek","H1834","HNpl","Damascus"],["הִנֵּה","hineh","H2009","HTj","there!"],["דַמֶּשֶׂק","damesek","H1834","HNpl","Damascus"],["מוּסָר","musar","H5493","HVHsmsa","[is] about to be removed"],["מֵעִיר","me'ir","H5892","HR/Ncfsa","from a city"],["וְהָיְתָה","vehayetah","H1961","Hc/Vqq3fs","and it will be"],["מְעִי","me'i","H4596","HNcmsc","a ruin of"],["מַפָּלָה","mapalah","H4654","HNcfsa","a ruin"]],"x":[[30001003,30001005,6],[23025002,23025002,5],[38009001,38009001,5],[1014015,1014015,3],[23007008,23007008,3],[24049002,24049002,3],[24049023,24049027,3],[33001006,33001006,3],[44009002,44009002,3]],"xn":9},"2":{"w":[["עֲזֻבוֹת","azuvot","H5800","HVqsfpa","[will be] abandoned"